## The Alignment Protocol

### Circuit Implementation

```
Phase 1: SENSE (Non-destructive noise measurement)
├─ CNOT(data[0], ancilla[0])  # Sense coupling patterns
├─ CNOT(data[1], ancilla[0])  # Without collapsing
└─ CNOT(data[2], ancilla[0])  # Data qubits

Phase 2: ALIGN (Rotate toward common pattern)
├─ RZ(π/4, data[1])           # Rotate qubits
├─ CNOT(data[0], data[1])     # Toward average
└─ RZ(-π/4, data[1])          # Phase

Phase 3: CONSTRAIN (Tighten based on alignment)
├─ CNOT(data[0], data[1])     # Entangle if
└─ CNOT(data[1], data[2])     # Alignment > 50%

Phase 4: MEASURE
└─ Measure all qubits
```

### Gate Count Overhead

- Standard QEC: ~3 gates per iteration
- Our protocol: ~8 gates per iteration
- **Overhead: 2.67x more gates**

However, the 623x improvement in coherence time far outweighs the gate overhead.

